# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE DATA — never publish.
#
# my-materials/ holds real CVs, referees' names, submitted applications and
# personal identifiers. proteus/data/ and proteus/out/ hold the identity graph,
# the database and generated drafts built from them. None of it belongs on
# GitHub. Only the engine and the sample data are public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
my-materials/
proteus/databases/
proteus/out/
proteus/data/seed_identity.json
proteus/data/seed_identity.backup.json
proteus/data/master_cv.txt
proteus/data/materials_manifest.json
proteus/data/real_jobs/
proteus/data/relative_to_opportunity_statement.md
# Personal working logs. DECISIONS.md records the real job hunt — job IDs,
# rejections, salary figures, visa details — and PROPOSALS.md its open
# questions. Both now live in my-materials/reference/ and are ignored there.
proteus/data/calibration_levels.json


# Keep the templates and samples that make the repo usable by someone else.
!proteus/data/seed_identity.template.json
!proteus/data/sample_jobs/

# The secret list itself. Publishing a list of exactly what you are hiding
# would defeat the point.
.githooks/secrets.txt

# Working rules that describe one real job hunt.
CLAUDE.md

# Local machine config — contains the local username in absolute paths.
.claude/settings.local.json

